<subheader>Synchronization Data Storage</subheader>

Once CSPro connects to a file-based synchronization service, it looks for or creates a directory named <i>CSPro</i> in the root directory, using it for the results of synchronization operations. CSPro uses the following directories:

<table 2 header nowrap>
    <cell>Directory</cell><cell>Description</cell>
    <cell><b>/</b></cell><cell>Files accessed using <logiccolor>syncfile</logiccolor> are evaluated from the root directory, not the <i>CSPro</i> directory.~!~&nbsp;</cell>
    <cell><b>/CSPro/apps/</b></cell><cell>Applications <link CSDeploy::introduction_to_deployment.csdoc>deployed</link> and used in operations such as <logiccolor>syncapp</logiccolor> or while <link CSDeploy::update_deployment_mobile.csdoc>updating applications</link>.~!~&nbsp;</cell>
    <cell><b>/CSPro/DataSync/</b></cell><cell>Case data uploaded using <logiccolor>syncdata</logiccolor>, and the <link data_dictionary_file_dcf.csdoc>dictionary</link> describing it, are stored in subdirectories named using the dictionary's <link syncable_name.csdoc>syncable name</link>. For example: <i>/CSPro/DataSync/LFS<definition System::year />_DICT/data/</i> and <i>/CSPro/DataSync/LFS<definition System::year />_DICT/dict/</i>.~!~&nbsp;</cell>
    <cell><b>/CSPro/messages/</b></cell><cell>Messages sent using <logiccolor>syncmessage</logiccolor>.~!~&nbsp;</cell>
    <cell><b>/CSPro/paradata/</b></cell><cell><link paradata.csdoc>Paradata</link> logs uploaded using <logiccolor>syncparadata</logiccolor> or <action>Sync.syncParadata</action>.</cell>
</table>
